pture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨2,-1,6⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,10⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -2x+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275237" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14617.json" "file_sha256" "c3a63a80d8ab0c39b4c570d4a22b16632363e70b7b40672ceaec9fe25d81d337" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14617.json" "file_sha256" "c3a63a80d8ab0c39b4c570d4a22b16632363e70b7b40672ceaec9fe25d81d337" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14618.json" "file_sha256" "7f6b5ddcdf9d1ec55dce58c09b66fdd24e34b716af18e02ebf61f4ec219ffe24" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14618.json" "file_sha256" "7f6b5ddcdf9d1ec55dce58c09b66fdd24e34b716af18e02ebf61f4ec219ffe24" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14619.json" "file_sha256" "fa1135cc133105c7e5c1749a8d5dacd867180d7702004b284fd60ace6f3f8eb1" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/example-14619.json" "file_sha256" "fa1135cc133105c7e5c1749a8d5dacd867180d7702004b284fd60ace6f3f8eb1" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,-2,5⟩$ and $b=⟨3,-1,-1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "056e6473653a5de077699a6108bca9577ebe0afa46b5d5f93f7a5d7b1ec082cd" "basis" 882 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "056e6473653a5de077699a6108bca9577ebe0afa46b5d5f93f7a5d7b1ec082cd" "basis" 882 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ef08c4fd09268676b82664916c9763be3840951a84d1e4516266193f35f9c7b" "basis" 882 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "056e6473653a5de077699a6108bca9577ebe0afa46b5d5f93f7a5d7b1ec082cd" "basis" 882 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "056e6473653a5de077699a6108bca9577ebe0afa46b5d5f93f7a5d7b1ec082cd" "basis" 882 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{30}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}⟩"]