stion-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "09c4e9e75cb7d729d2e11e094e4696bf71f2a366dbdd2f311fc7ee6c208936b7" "basis" 1072 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "09c4e9e75cb7d729d2e11e094e4696bf71f2a366dbdd2f311fc7ee6c208936b7" "basis" 1072 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "09c4e9e75cb7d729d2e11e094e4696bf71f2a366dbdd2f311fc7ee6c208936b7" "basis" 1072 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{1}{9}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "09c4e9e75cb7d729d2e11e094e4696bf71f2a366dbdd2f311fc7ee6c208936b7" "basis" 1072 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "09c4e9e75cb7d729d2e11e094e4696bf71f2a366dbdd2f311fc7ee6c208936b7" "basis" 1072 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-316436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,m\\,|=12$, $|\\,n\\,|=9$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $m$ onto $n$ in terms of the vector $n.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{n}\\,m=$\n{{field-1}}\n$n$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-316436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m & =|\\,m\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $n:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}=\\frac{n}{9}=\\frac{1}{9}n\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{n}\\,m & ={\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m\\cdot u \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}n \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}n\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-316436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6fe8f0b00258bee9b2b21577475e5a48381bafc9b7690de1fb8c376e61486fc"} {"question" "q-316436" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-316436" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=10$, $|\\,d\\,|=2\\sqrt{3}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}d\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6fe8f0b00258bee9b2b21577475e5a48381bafc9b7690de1fb8c376e61486fc"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5d"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}d"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}d"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}d"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}d"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}d"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=8$, $|\\,d\\,|=5$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}d \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\,d\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6fe8f0b00258bee9b2b21577475e5a48381bafc9b7690de1fb8c376e61486fc"} {"question" "q-275226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-18375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=6$, $|\\,b\\,|=2$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-18375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $b:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{b}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}b\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}b\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-18375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6fe8f0b00258bee9b2b21577475e5a48381bafc9b7690de1fb8c376e61486fc"} {"question" "q-18375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-18375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}b"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}b"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}b"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}b"] ["math" "b"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-18375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}b"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=4\\sqrt{2}$, $|\\,q\\,|=16$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{4\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p \\\\  & =2p\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6fe8f0b00258bee9b2b21577475e5a48381bafc9b7690de1fb8c376e61486fc"} {"question" "q-71839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4p"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}p"] ["math" "2p"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}p"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}p"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-71839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2p"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 7+8\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1}{{7}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{54}⟨7,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}⟨7,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6fe8f0b00258bee9b2b21577475e5a48381bafc9b7690de1fb8c376e61486fc"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{7}{54},\\frac{2}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{7}{54},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{1}{9}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨2,-1,6⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,10⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/state.json" "file_sha256" "019c2b25f329e6c9df6ac453626d05fd762f0bbe3a38ed201401092e46827f55"} {"question" "q-275230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/li